```java
import java.util.Scanner;

public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Scanner scanner = new Scanner(System.in);
        
        // Get the number of elements from the user
        System.out.println("Enter the number of elements:");
        int n = scanner.nextInt();
        
        // Generate HTML head and tail based on the input
        String htmlHead = generateHtmlHead(n, offset);
        String htmlTail = generateHtmlTail(n, offset);
        
        // Print the generated HTML head and tail
        System.out.println("HTML Head:");
        System.out.println(htmlHead);
        System.out.println("HTML Tail:");
        System.out.println(htmlTail);
    }

    /**
     * Generates HTML head based on the number of elements.
     *
     * @param n The number of elements.
     * @param offset An optional parameter for offset generation
     * @return The generated HTML head.
     */
    public static String generateHtmlHead(int n, int offset) {
        StringBuilder htmlHead = new StringBuilder();
        
        // Add the title
        if (offset != 0) {
            htmlHead.append("<title>My Page</title>");
        } else {
            htmlHead.append("<title>My Page");
        }
        
        // Add the meta tags
        htmlHead.append("<meta charset='UTF-8'>\n");
        htmlHead.append("<meta name='viewport' content='width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0'>\n");
        htmlHead.append("<link rel='stylesheet' href='styles.css'>\n");
        
        return htmlHead.toString();
    }

    /**
     * Generates HTML tail based on the number of elements.
     *
     * @param n The number of elements.
     * @return The generated HTML tail.
     */
    public static String generateHtmlTail(int n) {
        StringBuilder htmlTail = new StringBuilder();
        
        // Add a closing tag for the HTML body
        htmlTail.append("</body></html>\n");
        
        return htmlTail.toString();
    }
}
```

This code will prompt the user to enter the number of elements, and then it will generate the HTML head and tail based on that input. The `generateHtmlHead` function adds a title, meta tags for character encoding and viewport size, and a link to an external stylesheet. The `generateHtmlTail` function simply adds a closing tag for the HTML body.

Please note that this is just one possible way to solve the problem, and you can modify it according to your specific requirements.
